## Candidate and invariants

`diagnostics/direct-bg-dynamic-upper/reproduce/slot-upper.jl` implements exactly
one Float64 value per live slot, six Int slot arrays, four inverse-order maps and
four head/tail vectors. Free slots use row_id=0 and column_next as the free link;
other metadata/value is cleared. No persistent dictionary, per-row vector or
second coefficient representation. Handles remain internal.

Construction validates square CSC structure and q before publication. It visits
stable original-basis IDs in order, through inverse q, preserving signed explicit
zeros/NaN bits and ordered row/column lists. Link checks the supplied neighboring
gaps in constant work; no duplicate full lookup or full checker in mutations.
Known-slot stores delete exact zeros only. Swap merges the two sorted row lists;
rotation relinks the moving physical row through affected column intervals before
changing logical maps. Coefficient values/physical IDs do not move.

Growth uses checked max(required,C+max(C div2,16)), not a generic 1.5x claim at
small C:0→16,16→32,24→40. It creates all seven buffers before publication, copies
all old slot IDs/links and attaches new free slots to the old free chain. A private
call-local allocator seam is used only for planned failure injection; its contract
requires fresh independent vectors, it is never retained. There is no global hook.
No whole-update rollback promise or factor/solve behavior is introduced by Task1.

