## Work, allocation and retained-memory review

At setup: q validation/inverse O(n), CSC validation/import O(n+nnz),15 vector
buffers plus the arena object. The retained payload is56*C+64*n bytes on64-bit,
plus array/object headers/scalars. No coefficient-level object allocations.
Local lookup costs row degree; link/unlink/set have constant metadata work except
reserve. Swap costs sum of row degrees; rotation costs moved-row affected-column
interval traversal plus map rotation length. No solver kernels are called.

Growth allocates seven replacement vectors; old and new payloads coexist until
publication and collection. It initializes buffers and copies seven old prefixes;
free capacity remains retained after deletion, and no compaction occurs. The full
checker/selected-state/permutation oracle allocate only in the diagnostic tests.
No runtime allocation-free or speedup claim: pointer chasing and link capacity can
outweigh avoided packed shifts. Exact hidden Julia allocation behavior is not
qualified by textual absence of allocation calls.

The remaining Task2 adapter must preserve the accepted BG arithmetic, caches,
